Requirements
- Python 3
- Packages listed in requirements.txt (including Pygame)
Setup and Run
Open a terminal in the project root --- the folder containing main.py
and requirements.txt --- and run:
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
python main.py
If your system uses py to launch Python on Windows, you can use:
py -m pip install -r requirements.txt
py main.py
Testing Checklist
Use these checks to verify the game behavior:
- [ ] The game launches without a Python import or file-path error.
- [ ] The ball bounces off the left, right, and top walls.
- [ ] Paddle collisions redirect the ball and the ball does not pass
  through the paddle during normal play.
- [ ] Brick collisions destroy a brick and increase the score.
- [ ] A side collision produces a horizontal bounce when appropriate.
- [ ] Losing all lives displays GAME OVER and the final score.
- [ ] Destroying all bricks displays YOU WIN! and the final score.
- [ ] The game stops updating after the end state.
- [ ] Pressing a key after the end screen returns to the difficulty
  menu.
- [ ] Easy, Medium, and Hard can each be selected.
- [ ] Sound effects play for brick hits, paddle hits, and lost lives
  when audio is available.
- [ ] Esc exits the game.
Commit Summary
The repository history includes the following implementation and cleanup
changes:
- Fix ball collision detection --- Resolves collisions according
  to the side of the brick or paddle that the ball hits.
- Add game over screen and final score --- Adds win/loss states,
  an end-screen overlay, and final-score display.
- Add replay and difficulty selection --- Adds Easy, Medium, and
  Hard modes and a menu flow for replaying.
- Add sound effects for game events --- Adds sound feedback for
  brick hits, paddle hits, and lost lives.
- Ignore Python cache files --- Keeps generated Python cache files
  out of version control.
